          "block_content": "10  $ \\mu $m pinhole it flattened out the beam profile across the entrance pupil of the objective lens. The frequency doubled beam was polarized by a Glan–Thomson prism with a polarization ratio of  $ 10^{-6} $. A zero-order  $ \\lambda/2 $-plate mounted on a stepping motor precisely rotated the orientation of the incoming field with respect to the layer.",
